---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Mac Remote Controller">
	<article class="legal-page">
		<div class="container">
			<header class="legal-header">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="last-updated">Effective Date: February 2, 2026<br>Last Updated: February 2026</p>
			</header>

			<div class="legal-content">
				<section>
					<h2>1. Overview</h2>
					<p>
						Mac Remote Controller is a utility application that allows users to control their Mac computer using an Android device. The app operates over a local Wi-Fi network and requires the companion software "Mac Remote Controller Desktop" installed on the user's Mac computer.
					</p>
					<p>
						Mac Remote Controller ("we", "our", or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our mobile application, Mac companion application, and website.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>2. Data Collection</h2>
					<p>
						We respect your privacy. Mac Remote Controller does not require an account, and the core local-network remote control features work without you providing personal information.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>No account or login is required</strong> - The app works entirely offline on your local network</li>
						<li><strong>No user content is uploaded by core features</strong> - Remote control operates within your local environment</li>
						<li><strong>We do not access your contacts, photos, or files</strong> for the core remote-control functionality</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>2.1 Android App: SDK Data (Firebase / AdMob)</h3>
					<p>
						The Android app uses third-party SDKs (such as Google Firebase and Google Mobile Ads / AdMob). These SDKs may automatically collect and process certain data types, including identifiers that Google Play may classify as “Device or other IDs”.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Device or other IDs:</strong> e.g., Advertising ID and/or Firebase installation/app instance identifiers</li>
						<li><strong>App activity / interactions:</strong> analytics events about how the app is used</li>
						<li><strong>App info and performance:</strong> crash logs and diagnostics (e.g., via Crashlytics)</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						This data is used to provide analytics, diagnose crashes, and (where applicable) serve ads. These services may process data on our behalf, and in some cases data is shared with Google as part of providing these services.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Firebase Analytics</strong> (Google)</li>
						<li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> (Google)</li>
						<li><strong>Google Mobile Ads (AdMob)</strong></li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						You can manage ad personalization and identifiers through your Android device settings (for example, resetting or limiting the Advertising ID) and through your Google account ad settings. You can also uninstall the app at any time.
					</p>
					
					<h3>2.2 Mac Desktop Download: Optional Registration</h3>
					<p>
						You can download the Mac Remote Controller Desktop app without registering. If you choose to register to <strong>join our user base</strong>, we collect your email address and associate it with basic download metadata.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Email address</strong> (only if you choose to register)</li>
						<li><strong>Downloaded file/version</strong> (e.g., filename/version)</li>
						<li><strong>Download count</strong> and <strong>timestamps</strong> (created/last download time)</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						We use registered emails to build our user base and to share product updates, including announcements about advantages and special features. We do not sell your email address. You can request deletion of your email record by contacting us at the email address in the Contact Us section.
					</p>

					<h3>2.3 Website Analytics</h3>
					<p>
						Our website uses analytics services to understand how visitors interact with our website. These services collect anonymous usage statistics only after you grant consent via our cookie consent banner.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Necessary Analytics (Umami):</strong> We use Umami, a privacy-focused analytics service that collects minimal, anonymized data. Umami does not use cookies and respects Do Not Track headers. The data collected includes:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Page views (anonymized)</li>
						<li>Download events (to track successful and blocked download attempts)</li>
						<li>General device and browser information</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						<strong>Optional Analytics (Firebase Analytics and Microsoft Clarity):</strong> When you choose "Allow All" in our cookie consent banner, we also use:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Firebase Analytics (Google):</strong> Collects page views, navigation patterns, download button clicks, general location data (country/region level, not precise location), and device type and browser information.</li>
						<li><strong>Microsoft Clarity:</strong> A behavioral analytics tool that provides session recordings, heatmaps, and insights into how users interact with our website. Clarity collects anonymized data including mouse movements, clicks, scroll depth, and page interactions to help us understand user behavior and improve website usability.</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						You can control analytics loading through our consent banner. If you choose “Only Necessary”, we only load Umami; if you choose “Allow All”, we also load Firebase Analytics and Microsoft Clarity.
					</p>
					
					<h3>2.4 Cookie Consent</h3>
					<p>
						We use a cookie consent system that allows you to choose between:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Only Necessary:</strong> Only Umami Analytics (privacy-focused, minimal data collection)</li>
						<li><strong>Allow All:</strong> Umami Analytics, Firebase Analytics, and Microsoft Clarity</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						Your consent preference is stored locally in your browser and is respected on all pages. You can change your preference at any time by clearing your browser cookies and revisiting our website.
					</p>
					
					<h3>2.5 Local Network Communication</h3>
					<p>
						The Mac Remote Controller app’s remote-control traffic operates over your local network. Communication for controlling your Mac occurs directly between your Android device and your Mac on your local network. Separately, the Android app may send analytics/ads/crash data to third-party providers as described in Section 2.1.
					</p>
					
					<h3>2.6 Device Information</h3>
					<p>
						The application may access device information necessary for establishing local network connections, such as IP addresses and network identifiers. This information is used solely for the purpose of establishing connections between your devices and is not stored or transmitted outside your local network.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>3. Permissions</h2>
					<p>
						To function correctly, the Mac Remote Controller app may request access to:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Wi-Fi / Network Access:</strong> Used solely to discover and connect to the server application on your Mac over your local network</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						These permissions are used <strong>only</strong> for local communication between your Android device and Mac computer. No local-control traffic is sent to our servers. Depending on the features you use, the Android app may also include optional components such as analytics/ads SDKs (see Section 2.1).
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
					<p>
						Any information collected is used solely to:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Email Addresses (optional):</strong> If you register to join our user base, we store your email and associate it with Mac desktop download metadata</li>
						<li><strong>User base communications:</strong> If you register, we may contact you with product updates, including announcements about advantages and special features</li>
						<li><strong>Application Data:</strong> Establish and maintain connections between your Android device and Mac, and enable remote control functionality</li>
						<li><strong>Analytics / Ads SDK Data (Android app):</strong> Improve performance and reliability, measure usage, and (where applicable) serve ads</li>
						<li><strong>Website Analytics Data:</strong> Improve our website and understand website usage patterns</li>
						<li><strong>Device Information:</strong> Enable local network communication and improve app functionality</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>5. Data Storage</h2>
					<p>
						<strong>Application Data:</strong> Core remote-control preferences/settings remain on your devices. We do not operate an account system for the mobile or Mac apps. Separately, third-party SDKs in the Android app (if enabled/used) may collect and store analytics/ads/crash data as described in Section 2.1.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Mac Download Email Data (Optional):</strong> If you register to join our user base when downloading the Mac desktop app, we store your email securely on our backend servers hosted on Railway along with download metadata (filename/version, download count, timestamps). This data is encrypted in transit. You can request deletion of your email data at any time by contacting us.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Website Analytics Data:</strong> Website analytics data is stored by the respective analytics providers (Umami, Google Firebase Analytics, and Microsoft Clarity) in accordance with their privacy policies.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Android SDK Data:</strong> Analytics/ads/crash data collected by third-party SDKs (Firebase/AdMob/Crashlytics) is stored and processed by those providers in accordance with their privacy policies.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
					<p>
						Our website, Android app, and download system may use the following third-party services:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Railway:</strong> Hosts our backend server for email collection and download metadata. See <a href="https://railway.app/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Railway's Privacy Policy</a></li>
						<li><strong>Umami Analytics:</strong> Privacy-focused analytics service for website usage statistics. Umami does not use cookies and respects Do Not Track. See <a href="https://umami.is/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Umami's Privacy Policy</a></li>
						<li><strong>Firebase Analytics (Google):</strong> Optional website usage analytics (only when you choose "Allow All"). See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a></li>
						<li><strong>Microsoft Clarity:</strong> Optional behavioral analytics service that provides session recordings and heatmaps (only when you choose "Allow All"). See <a href="https://clarity.microsoft.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Clarity's Terms of Service</a> and <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft's Privacy Statement</a></li>
						<li><strong>Google Mobile Ads (AdMob):</strong> May be used in the Android app to serve ads. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a></li>
						<li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics (Google):</strong> May be used in the Android app for crash reporting. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a></li>
						<li><strong>Google Play Store:</strong> For app distribution. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a></li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						We encourage you to review the privacy policies of these third-party services.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>7. Data Security</h2>
					<p>
						Core remote-control communication happens over your local network. For our website and backend services, we use standard security measures and encrypt data in transit (HTTPS) where applicable.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
					<p>
						Our application is not intended for children under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you are under 13, please do not register (join our user base) or provide an email address on our website.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
					<p>
						You have the right to:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Use the mobile and Mac applications without providing personal information</li>
						<li>Control all data stored locally on your devices</li>
						<li>Control cookie and analytics consent via our consent banner</li>
						<li>Opt out of website analytics using our consent banner</li>
						<li>Manage Android ad personalization/identifiers through your device settings (where applicable)</li>
						<li>Request deletion of your Mac download email data by contacting us</li>
						<li>Uninstall the app at any time, which removes all locally stored data</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						If you wish to have your Mac download email data deleted, please contact us at the email address provided in the Contact Us section.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
					<p>
						We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make any changes, we will update the "Effective Date" at the top of this page and post the updated policy on this page. You are encouraged to review this Privacy Policy periodically to stay informed about how we protect your information.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
					<p>
						If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:macremotecontroller@gmail.com">macremotecontroller@gmail.com</a>
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Company:</strong> AG-sound Denmark<br>
						<strong>Copyright © 2025</strong>
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.legal-page {
		padding: 2rem 1rem;
		min-height: 100vh;
	}

	.container {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.legal-header {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
		text-align: center;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
		padding-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.legal-header h1 {
		font-size: 3rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
		-webkit-background-clip: text;
		-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
		background-clip: text;
	}

	.last-updated {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
		font-size: 0.875rem;
	}

	.legal-content {
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	.legal-content section {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.legal-content h2 {
		font-size: 1.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		color: white;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.legal-content h3 {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
	}

	.legal-content p {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.legal-content ul {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
		margin-left: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.legal-content li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.legal-content a {
		color: #667eea;
		text-decoration: underline;
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	.legal-content a:hover {
		color: #764ba2;
	}

	.legal-content strong {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	@media (min-width: 768px) {
		.legal-page {
			padding: 4rem 2rem;
		}
	}
</style>

